# Find an Effect
<!--{ "parent": "magic", "order": 0 }-->

*Every application, all 23 Fundamentals, in one searchable list — for when you know the effect you want but not which Fundamental hides it. Type a word from the name or the description; click an application to read it in context on its Fundamental's page.*

<!-- all-applications -->
<div class="entity-view">
<style>
.ev-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:0 0 1.5em;font-size:.92em}
.ev-table th,.ev-table td{border:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,.3);padding:.35em .5em;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}
.ev-table th{font-size:.78em;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em}
.ev-cards{display:grid;gap:1em;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(260px,1fr))}
.ev-card{border:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,.3);border-radius:8px;padding:.75em 1em;break-inside:avoid;page-break-inside:avoid}
.ev-card h3{margin:0 0 .4em}
.ev-img{display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;margin:0 0 .5em}
.ev-fields{margin:0 0 .6em}
.ev-fields dt{display:inline;font-size:.78em;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;opacity:.65}
.ev-fields dt::after{content:": "}
.ev-fields dd{display:inline;margin:0}
.ev-fields dd::after{content:"";display:block}
.ev-body{margin:0}
.ev-bar{display:flex;gap:.5em;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:0 0 .75em}
.ev-toggle,.ev-chip{border:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,.4);background:transparent;color:inherit;border-radius:999px;padding:.2em .7em;cursor:pointer;font:inherit;font-size:.85em}
.ev-toggle[aria-pressed="true"],.ev-chip[aria-pressed="true"]{background:rgba(128,128,128,.25);font-weight:600}
.ev-search{flex:1;min-width:8em;font:inherit;padding:.25em .5em;border:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,.4);border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:inherit}
.ev-empty{opacity:.7;font-style:italic}
.ev-count{font-size:.85em;opacity:.65;white-space:nowrap}
</style>
<foresight-table filter placeholder="Search all 232 applications…"><table class="ev-table"><thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>Fundamental</th><th align="center">Int</th><th align="center">§</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-search="abeyance abeyance delay the whole or a part of the magical effect of which this application is part by up to one day (controlled or fixed, bestowed)."><td><a href="/magic-abeyance/#app-abeyance">Abeyance</a></td><td><a href="/magic-abeyance/">Abeyance</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§1B2</td></tr><tr data-search="age time increase or reduce the age of a target by up to ten years. (targets made older are aged, while those made younger also lose experience, skills, etc. ie. when a target's age is reduced by x years, it becomes as it was x years ago, whereas increasing a target's age does not make it as it will be in x years, but as it might be were it to lie around — doing nothing and having nothing done to it — for that time.) note that this application, as stated, is temporary, and reverses once the effect is ended (either by running out of time or being dispelled)."><td><a href="/magic-time/#app-age">Age</a></td><td><a href="/magic-time/">Time</a></td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">§23A6</td></tr><tr data-search="agonizing touch touch inflict or remove a sensation equal to a large impact, a large creature's bite, a mighty blow, a coronary, a st15 grasp/push, or the effects of a class c or p1 poison (dc8, controlled)."><td><a href="/magic-touch/#app-agonizing-touch">Agonizing Touch</a></td><td><a href="/magic-touch/">Touch</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§21A5</td></tr><tr data-search="alter seas water alter conditions in a 1km radius by shifting the conditions by (at most) one row on each of the two columns below. | wind | seas | |---|---| | calm | glassy | | slight breeze | calm | | gusty breeze | low swell | | moderate wind | moderate swell | | strong wind | large swell | | storm wind | stormy seas | | gale | rending seas | | hurricane | tidal waves | | tornado | | note: wind direction may be altered by up to 45° (eg. from se to e) instead of altering its intensity. also note that while the duration of this effect is only five minutes, the return to normality will be gradual (as though the artificially brought conditions had come about naturally)."><td><a href="/magic-water/#app-alter-seas">Alter Seas</a></td><td><a href="/magic-water/">Water</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§24A8</td></tr><tr data-search="alter weather air alter the weather within a 1km radius by shifting the weather's description by one row on each of the three columns below. while the duration of this effect is only two minutes, the return to normality will be gradual (as though the artificially invoked conditions had come about naturally). | temperature | wind | precipitation | |---|---|---| | -50°c | calm | none | | -30°c | slight breeze | fog | | -10°c | gusty breeze | drizzle | | 5°c | moderate wind | medium rain | | 20°c | strong wind | heavy rain | | 30°c | storm wind | rivers flood levies | | 40°c | gale | flash floods | | 50°c | hurricane | (or hail or snow if applicable) | | 60°c | tornado | | note: wind direction may be altered by up to 45° (eg. from se to e) instead of altering its intensity."><td><a href="/magic-air/#app-alter-weather">Alter Weather</a></td><td><a href="/magic-air/">Air</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§2A10</td></tr><tr data-search="amplification dimension increase/decrease any one numerical constraint on the effects of an application which is part of the same effect as this application by up to 50%. this application may not be used to modify the parameters of (this or other) applications of the expansion fundamental, nor to alter the duration of an effect. (bestowed.)"><td><a href="/magic-dimension/#app-amplification">Amplification</a></td><td><a href="/magic-dimension/">Dimension</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§10A4</td></tr><tr data-search="animal noises sound animal noises — roars, barks, clip-clops, neighs, etc. (controlled)."><td><a href="/magic-sound/#app-animal-noises">Animal Noises</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sound/">Sound</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§19B7</td></tr><tr data-search="animate dead summon animate the corpse or skeleton of a dt1 or weaker creature (by summoning a trivial demon for the purpose) as a zombie or skeleton respectively (see the creature descriptions). note: the figures given (under creatures) for zombies/skeletons assume that (near-)human skeletons/corpses are being animated. if the original creature had dt d, then the skeleton/zombie will have dt d-3 / d+1, and dc d+1 / d+2. the gm may wish to make special allowance for non-humanoid skeletons/zombies. also note that skeletons and zombies are intrinsically hostile to any living creature (including their summoner). corpses/skeletons without intact heads/skulls cannot be animated."><td><a href="/magic-summon/#app-animate-dead">Animate Dead</a></td><td><a href="/magic-summon/">Summon</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§20A4</td></tr><tr data-search="animate plant wood animate a plant no larger than 2m×2m×2m. it will have the fighting abilities and mobility of a zombie, with dt = height in m, and dc = height in m + 1."><td><a href="/magic-wood/#app-animate-plant">Animate Plant</a></td><td><a href="/magic-wood/">Wood</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§25A6</td></tr><tr data-search="animate stone earth animate a statue of a living creature ≤2m×2m×2m. the animated statue acts in every way like the &quot;real thing&quot;, with the exception of magical and similar special capabilities; other special effects, such as those of poisons, disappear once the animating effect's duration expires (bestowed)."><td><a href="/magic-earth/#app-animate-stone">Animate Stone</a></td><td><a href="/magic-earth/">Earth</a></td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">§8A12</td></tr><tr data-search="animation apportation fully animate a flexible object massing no more than one kilogram as though it were a live creature (with st equal to 2, ag and dx at most equal to those of the invoker; controlled)."><td><a href="/magic-apportation/#app-animation">Animation</a></td><td><a href="/magic-apportation/">Apportation</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§3A6</td></tr><tr data-search="ask divination gain a single-word reply (you can call it an answer if you're optimistic) to a question of the invoker's choice. if the answer cannot be expressed in one word, or if the question is poorly defined (eg. if the gm can't understand it, or doesn't want to answer it), then no reply is forthcoming. (range: infinite.)* !!!"><td><a href="/magic-divination/#app-ask">Ask</a></td><td><a href="/magic-divination/">Divination</a></td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">§7A13</td></tr><tr data-search="ball of fire fire create a fiery explosion (immediate, bestowed): - dc5 to anyone in the hex targeted; - dc4 to those in hexes adjacent to that hex; - dc2 to those in hexes two hexes from it."><td><a href="/magic-fire/#app-ball-of-fire">Ball of Fire</a></td><td><a href="/magic-fire/">Fire</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§12A5</td></tr><tr data-search="ball of light image create a glowing ball up to 20cm in diameter, of any colour (controlled)."><td><a href="/magic-image/#app-ball-of-light">Ball of Light</a></td><td><a href="/magic-image/">Image</a></td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">§13B2</td></tr><tr data-search="beam of light image cause a flashlight-equivalent beam of light, good for 20m, to emanate from one's finger (controlled)."><td><a href="/magic-image/#app-beam-of-light">Beam of Light</a></td><td><a href="/magic-image/">Image</a></td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">§13B1</td></tr><tr data-search="bestow heightened sense sense as heighten sense (§16b2), but bestowed — the recipient now owns and controls the heightened sense themselves: it persists independently of you and your range, and you can neither sustain nor switch it off. (sense offers a bestowed form one intensity above the controlled one. bestowal is granted per-application, not a universal option — for many effects it would be badly unbalancing.)"><td><a href="/magic-sense/#app-bestow-heightened-sense">Bestow Heightened Sense</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sense/">Sense</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§16A3</td></tr><tr data-search="bestow replacement sense sense as replace sense (§16a4), but bestowed — the recipient owns and controls the new sense themselves, independent of you and your range. (bestowing costs +1 intensity over the controlled version.)"><td><a href="/magic-sense/#app-bestow-replacement-sense">Bestow Replacement Sense</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sense/">Sense</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§16A5</td></tr><tr data-search="bestow sense sense bestow a target with a human sense, and search and scan pcss (if none are possessed) of 5, +5 per sense bestowed (fixed, bestowed). possible senses: eyesight, hearing, touch, taste, smell, balance."><td><a href="/magic-sense/#app-bestow-sense">Bestow Sense</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sense/">Sense</a></td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">§16B1</td></tr><tr data-search="bestow true sight sense confer the ability to see one's surroundings free of all magically induced sensory data, and complete with any magically subdued sensory data (bestowed)."><td><a href="/magic-sense/#app-bestow-true-sight">Bestow True Sight</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sense/">Sense</a></td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">§16A8</td></tr><tr data-search="bestowed goldenear communication as goldenear (§5a4), but bestowed."><td><a href="/magic-communication/#app-bestowed-goldenear">Bestowed Goldenear</a></td><td><a href="/magic-communication/">Communication</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§5A6</td></tr><tr data-search="bestowed greater sound sound any intensity 2 application, bestowed."><td><a href="/magic-sound/#app-bestowed-greater-sound">Bestowed Greater Sound</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sound/">Sound</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§19A15</td></tr><tr data-search="bestowed image creation image any intensity 2 application, bestowed. clarification: &quot;remove&quot; image actually means to replace an image with what the invoker (controller) believes would be seen were that image not present (ie. not the same as making the object transparent, with the refractive index of air). so a character could not, for example, see through a door by &quot;removing&quot; its image. the invoker might put a sandestin with eyesight and remove image into the door, and then see through it…"><td><a href="/magic-image/#app-bestowed-image-creation">Bestowed Image Creation</a></td><td><a href="/magic-image/">Image</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§13A8</td></tr><tr data-search="bestowed image manipulation image any intensity 1 application, bestowed."><td><a href="/magic-image/#app-bestowed-image-manipulation">Bestowed Image Manipulation</a></td><td><a href="/magic-image/">Image</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§13A7</td></tr><tr data-search="bestowed lesser sound sound any intensity 0 application, bestowed."><td><a href="/magic-sound/#app-bestowed-lesser-sound">Bestowed Lesser Sound</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sound/">Sound</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§19B11</td></tr><tr data-search="bestowed light image any intensity 0 application, bestowed."><td><a href="/magic-image/#app-bestowed-light">Bestowed Light</a></td><td><a href="/magic-image/">Image</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§13B5</td></tr><tr data-search="bestowed silvertongue communication as silvertongue (§5a3), but bestowed."><td><a href="/magic-communication/#app-bestowed-silvertongue">Bestowed Silvertongue</a></td><td><a href="/magic-communication/">Communication</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§5A5</td></tr><tr data-search="bestowed sound sound any intensity 1 application, bestowed."><td><a href="/magic-sound/#app-bestowed-sound">Bestowed Sound</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sound/">Sound</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§19A14</td></tr><tr data-search="bind will compulsion bind the will of a target to that of the invoker, so that he/she does the invoker's bidding (but is otherwise free to do as he/she pleases). if faced with a highly traumatic situation, forced to do something abhorrent, or alien to its nature, the target may make a resistance roll: - qr1 — the binding is broken. - qr2 — he/she may ignore the instructions which led to the roll (and receives a +1 modifier to subsequent rolls). - qr3 — he/she hesitates (for one pulse) before continuing. - otherwise the roll has no effect. (duration infinite, fixed, bestowed.) !!!"><td><a href="/magic-compulsion/#app-bind-will">Bind Will</a></td><td><a href="/magic-compulsion/">Compulsion</a></td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">§6A11</td></tr><tr data-search="bolt of fire fire create a bolt of flame which may be manipulated as a dagger, although it inflicts dc5 (fire damage) on anyone cut by it, or holding it (fixed, bestowed)."><td><a href="/magic-fire/#app-bolt-of-fire">Bolt of Fire</a></td><td><a href="/magic-fire/">Fire</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§12B2</td></tr><tr data-search="buzzing sound buzzing (like that of a bee or fly) emanating from one point within range (controlled)."><td><a href="/magic-sound/#app-buzzing">Buzzing</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sound/">Sound</a></td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">§19B4</td></tr><tr data-search="carve wood wood the invoker may instantly transform a piece of wood into anything into which it could be made by skilled carpenters given time. (range: touch.)"><td><a href="/magic-wood/#app-carve-wood">Carve Wood</a></td><td><a href="/magic-wood/">Wood</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§25A7</td></tr><tr data-search="charm compulsion cause a character's demeanour to improve or worsen one row (eg. from neutral to friendly, or vice versa) at the invoker's option (fixed, bestowed)."><td><a href="/magic-compulsion/#app-charm">Charm</a></td><td><a href="/magic-compulsion/">Compulsion</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§6B1</td></tr><tr data-search="conditional sandestin sandestin as above, but the clauses may be conditional (including terms like &quot;if … then …&quot;, &quot;do … until …&quot;). however, the verification of conditions must be based upon some senses bestowed upon the sandestin (either as part of it, or subsequently) or it will assume that all conditional terms are false. eg. &quot;if you sense magic then glow blue&quot; (of course the sandestin would need some means to perceive magic — and know that that was what it was doing — and some means to glow blue, or it might go beep &quot;syntax error&quot;)."><td><a href="/magic-sandestin/#app-conditional-sandestin">Conditional Sandestin</a></td><td><a href="/magic-sandestin/">Sandestin</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§17B2</td></tr><tr data-search="cone of bloating water the invoker may create a cone of bloating with its base anywhere within range. the cone is 12m wide at its base and draws to a point at its invoker. those wholly or mostly within it suffer dc3 from becoming bloated with water (immediate)."><td><a href="/magic-water/#app-cone-of-bloating">Cone of Bloating</a></td><td><a href="/magic-water/">Water</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§24A7</td></tr><tr data-search="cone of heat air the invoker may create a cone of heat with its base anywhere within range. the cone is 20m wide at its base and draws to a point at its invoker. those wholly or mostly within it suffer dc3 from heat (immediate)."><td><a href="/magic-air/#app-cone-of-heat">Cone of Heat</a></td><td><a href="/magic-air/">Air</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§2A8</td></tr><tr data-search="cone of withering earth the invoker may create a cone of withering (this is a drying attack) with its base anywhere within range. the cone is 6m wide at its base and draws to a point at its invoker. those wholly or mostly within it suffer dc3 from drying (immediate)."><td><a href="/magic-earth/#app-cone-of-withering">Cone of Withering</a></td><td><a href="/magic-earth/">Earth</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§8A6</td></tr><tr data-search="confer understanding communication the invoker may make a target within range able to understand the speech of one other target within range for the duration of the effect (bestowed)."><td><a href="/magic-communication/#app-confer-understanding">Confer Understanding</a></td><td><a href="/magic-communication/">Communication</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§5B2</td></tr><tr data-search="confer understanding divination as divine text (§7b3), but bestowed."><td><a href="/magic-divination/#app-confer-understanding">Confer Understanding</a></td><td><a href="/magic-divination/">Divination</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§7A5</td></tr><tr data-search="conjure air air create a 5m×5m×5m volume of air in a space perhaps already occupied by air or vapour (but nothing denser). this volume may be decreased, but the air may not be compressed further. used judiciously, this spell creates gusts of wind, etc. (immediate)."><td><a href="/magic-air/#app-conjure-air">Conjure Air</a></td><td><a href="/magic-air/">Air</a></td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">§2B1</td></tr><tr data-search="contract wood wood contract a wooden object ≤2m×2m×2m by reducing its linear dimensions by up to 50%. the object's mass remains constant, while its strength and density increase markedly. - if armour is made out of such wood, it will be as metal armour of the equivalent type, but with protection values one worse in each category. - a weapon normally made of metal may be made of this material, but will have its dcs reduced by one. - a weapon normally made of wood may be made of this material, in which case its dcs are improved by one, while its mass is increased by 50%."><td><a href="/magic-wood/#app-contract-wood">Contract Wood</a></td><td><a href="/magic-wood/">Wood</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§25B3</td></tr><tr data-search="control feeling emotion instil or suppress in a character a built-up emotion such as courage, admiration, jealousy, trust, or anger (fixed, bestowed; duration: 1h)."><td><a href="/magic-emotion/#app-control-feeling">Control Feeling</a></td><td><a href="/magic-emotion/">Emotion</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§9A2</td></tr><tr data-search="control mood emotion instil or suppress in a character a transient emotion such as lust, puzzlement, hunger, fear, or distaste (fixed, bestowed; duration: 10min)."><td><a href="/magic-emotion/#app-control-mood">Control Mood</a></td><td><a href="/magic-emotion/">Emotion</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§9B1</td></tr><tr data-search="control passion emotion instil or suppress in a character a deep-seated emotion such as a phobia, loyalty, love, or hate (fixed, bestowed; duration: 1 day)."><td><a href="/magic-emotion/#app-control-passion">Control Passion</a></td><td><a href="/magic-emotion/">Emotion</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§9A3</td></tr><tr data-search="create earth earth create/remove a volume of earth, gravel, rock, or sand (at rest — eg. in a pile on the ground, but not in the air or on an object unable to support it) no larger than 5m×5m×5m (fixed)."><td><a href="/magic-earth/#app-create-earth">Create Earth</a></td><td><a href="/magic-earth/">Earth</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§8B2</td></tr><tr data-search="create gems earth create/remove a volume of gems occupying a volume no greater than 10cm×10cm×10cm."><td><a href="/magic-earth/#app-create-gems">Create Gems</a></td><td><a href="/magic-earth/">Earth</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§8A8</td></tr><tr data-search="create gold earth create/remove a volume of gold, lead, mercury, or other (lighter) metal, no larger than 20cm×20cm×20cm (fixed)."><td><a href="/magic-earth/#app-create-gold">Create Gold</a></td><td><a href="/magic-earth/">Earth</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§8A7</td></tr><tr data-search="create great water water create/remove 10,000 litres of water in a container or on the ground."><td><a href="/magic-water/#app-create-great-water">Create Great Water</a></td><td><a href="/magic-water/">Water</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§24B5</td></tr><tr data-search="create great wood wood create a piece of wood (equivalent to any naturally occurring kind) ≤1m×1m×20m."><td><a href="/magic-wood/#app-create-great-wood">Create Great Wood</a></td><td><a href="/magic-wood/">Wood</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§25A4</td></tr><tr data-search="create ice water create/remove 10,000 litres of ice in a container or on the ground."><td><a href="/magic-water/#app-create-ice">Create Ice</a></td><td><a href="/magic-water/">Water</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§24A6</td></tr><tr data-search="create portal apportation create a &quot;portal&quot;: a passage between a 3m×2m &quot;doorway&quot; within the invoker's range and another such &quot;doorway&quot; in some other place (chosen with as much accuracy as the invoker can muster) on this or another plane of existence. a creature entering one of the two &quot;doorways&quot; is instantly transported to the other. otherwise, the same notes apply to this application as apply to teleportal (§3a11). note that this application is not bestowed, so if used on its own, the portal collapses when its invoker passes through (assuming that the other end is out of range). !!! note: in both portal effects, the &quot;doorways&quot; appear as rectangles of blackness, with occasional flickers of colour. rays of light, sounds, and inanimate objects (unless carried or pushed by a creature) do not pass through. optional teleport &amp; gate rules. applications of apportation marked with an asterisk (*) receive the following modifications to their intensity: - do not change the intensity if the origin is extremely similar in both form and function to the destination. (eg. teleporting from one plush throne-room to another throne room of similar appearance; or opening a gate between two stone doorways of similar size and construction.) - add one to the intensity if the origin is similar in either shape or form to the destination. (eg. teleporting to a throne room from a barn decorated so as to resemble it; or opening a gate between a stone doorway leading into a corridor and another opening into an alcove.) - add two to the intensity if the origin and destination are not radically different. (eg. teleporting from an open field to a grassy knoll.) this also applies if the origin and destination are not very distinct locations — that is, land-marks or easily named locations. a room would be more &quot;distinct&quot; than a corridor, a crossroad more so than a road, a hill more so than a field. - add three (or more) to the intensity if the origin and destination are radically different. (eg. teleporting from the middle of a desert to the shore of a lake — you might add four to the intensity.)"><td><a href="/magic-apportation/#app-create-portal">Create Portal</a></td><td><a href="/magic-apportation/">Apportation</a></td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">§3A13</td></tr><tr data-search="create smoke air create a volume of thick smoke occupying a volume 5m×5m×5m (fixed)."><td><a href="/magic-air/#app-create-smoke">Create Smoke</a></td><td><a href="/magic-air/">Air</a></td><td 