/td><td align="center">150–1200</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">2500</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#weapon-machine-gun">Machine Gun</a></td><td>heavy</td><td align="center">11 B/P</td><td align="center">100–1500</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">4000</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#weapon-hand-grenade">Hand Grenade</a></td><td>thrown</td><td align="center">12 B</td><td align="center">thrown</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">40</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#weapon-laspistol">Laspistol</a></td><td>ranged</td><td align="center">8 B</td><td align="center">70–120</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">1k</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#weapon-laser-rifle">Laser Rifle</a></td><td>ranged</td><td align="center">10 B</td><td align="center">250–500</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">2k</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#weapon-stun-pistol">Stun Pistol</a></td><td>ranged</td><td align="center">6 stun</td><td align="center">16–20</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">700</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#weapon-cone-rifle">Cone Rifle</a></td><td>ranged</td><td align="center">13 B</td><td align="center">110–190</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">6c</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#weapon-autolasercannon">Autolasercannon</a></td><td>heavy</td><td align="center">14 B/P</td><td align="center">1.2k–1.5k</td><td align="center">8</td><td align="center">4k</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="ev-cards"><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-fist-kick"><h3>Fist / Kick</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>melee</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>2 I</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>touch</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Bare unarmed strike. The DC-4 anchor is an *inhuman* fist; an ordinary person lands about 2. Unarmed Combat skill does the rest.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-knife-dagger"><h3>Knife / Dagger</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>melee</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>4 M/P</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>touch</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>0.3</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Short blade — concealable, pierces armor, doubles as a tool and a thrown weapon. The floor of every weapon list.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-sword"><h3>Sword</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>melee</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>6 M</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>reach</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>1.3</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>60</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The arming sword — one-handed cut-and-thrust. *Fine*, *great*, and *short* are all adjectives on this one noun.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-greatsword"><h3>Greatsword</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>melee</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>8 M</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>long reach</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>2.7</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>120</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Two-handed blade. More reach and bite; no hand free for a shield.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-spear"><h3>Spear</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>melee</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>6 M/P</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>long reach</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>1.5</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Reach weapon that pierces. Set against a charge it counts double. A *thrown* spear is the same noun, one adjective.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-axe"><h3>Axe</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>melee</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>7 M</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>reach</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>1.4</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>30</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Heavy chopping edge — hits hard, harder to recover for a parry than a sword.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-mace-club"><h3>Mace / Club</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>melee</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>6 I</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>reach</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>1.4</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>25</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Impact rather than edge — cheap, and it doesn't care how good your armor's edge-turning is.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-quarterstaff"><h3>Quarterstaff</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>melee</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>4 I</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>long reach</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>1.1</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Two-handed staff: reach, a good Parry PM, and it's just a stick when the guards ask.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-bow"><h3>Bow</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>6 M/P</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>50–150</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>0.9</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>80</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Half-skill ranged weapon (Archery). Quiet, pierces, and only as good as the archer — the mundane benchmark magic is judged against.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-crossbow"><h3>Crossbow</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>7 M/P</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>40–120</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>1/2</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>2.5</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>150</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Point-and-hold power — trivial to aim, slow to span. Punches armor a bow can't.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-revolver"><h3>Revolver</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>8 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>12–60</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>300</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Reliable double-action sidearm; six shots, slow to reload. *Cut-down* makes it a concealable snub-nose.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-pistol-9mm"><h3>Pistol (9mm)</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>8 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>15–80</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>15</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>0.9</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>400</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The DC-8 anchor. Self-loading, high-capacity magazine — the default modern handgun.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-submachine-gun"><h3>Submachine Gun</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>8 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>20–120</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>[6]</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>30</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>600</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Pistol round, automatic fire. Devastating up close, thirsty and wild at range.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-shotgun"><h3>Shotgun</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>10 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>10–40</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>3.2</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>350</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Brutal and forgiving up close; falls off fast. *Cut-down* trades the last of its range for concealment.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-assault-rifle"><h3>Assault Rifle</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>10 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>50–300</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>[10]</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>30</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>3.6</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>900</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Intermediate cartridge, select fire — the standard modern long arm. *Carbine* is the light adjective.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-battle-rifle-7-62"><h3>Battle Rifle (7.62)</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>11 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>80–500</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>4.2</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>1000</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The DC-11 anchor. Full-power rifle round: range and penetration at the cost of weight and recoil.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-sniper-rifle"><h3>Sniper Rifle</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>12 B/P</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>150–1200</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>5.5</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>2500</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Precision, optics, and armor-piercing reach. A patient specialist's tool, not a firefight weapon.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-machine-gun"><h3>Machine Gun</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>heavy</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>11 B/P</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>100–1500</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>[20]</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>100</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>10</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>4000</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Belt-fed area denial — see Fire Combat. Emplaced or bipod; suppresses ground you never actually hit.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-hand-grenade"><h3>Hand Grenade</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>thrown</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>12 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>thrown</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>0.4</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>40</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Blast in a radius — no aim roll against a point, a scatter roll against an area. Fragmentation ignores light cover.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-laspistol"><h3>Laspistol</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>8 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>70–120</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>25</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>0.5</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>7</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>1k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Energy sidearm: no recoil, no ballistic drop, a power cell instead of a magazine. The SF echo of the 9mm.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-laser-rifle"><h3>Laser Rifle</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>10 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>250–500</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>50</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>7</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>2k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Line-of-sight beam weapon — flat trajectory, hungry for cells, dimmed by smoke and fog.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-stun-pistol"><h3>Stun Pistol</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>6 stun</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>16–20</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>15</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>7</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>700</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Non-lethal takedown — damage feeds a Pain Resistance / stun check rather than a wound. Short-ranged by design.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-cone-rifle"><h3>Cone Rifle</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>ranged</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>13 B</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>110–190</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>[6]</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>30</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>6c</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Fires micro-rockets — recoilless, heavy hitting, and it arcs, so cover is less help than you'd hope.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="weapon-autolasercannon"><h3>Autolasercannon</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Kind</dt><dd>heavy</dd><dt>PM</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Damage</dt><dd>14 B/P</dd><dt>Range</dt><dd>1.2k–1.5k</dd><dt>RoF</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Ammo</dt><dd>100</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>10</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>4k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Vehicle- or emplacement-scale beam weapon. Uses the Damage Scale rules — meant for things bigger than people.</p></section></div></div></foresight-table>
