</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">1200</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#armor-riot-gear">Riot Gear</a></td><td align="center">I4 M2</td><td align="center">−1 AG, −1 PC</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">800</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#armor-combat-armor">Combat Armor</a></td><td align="center">B5 M4 I4</td><td align="center">−1 PC</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">5k</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#armor-powered-armor">Powered Armor</a></td><td align="center">B6 M6 I6</td><td align="center">+AG, +ST</td><td align="center">8</td><td align="center">40k</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="ev-cards"><section class="ev-card" id="armor-padded-gambeson"><h3>Padded / Gambeson</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>torso, arms</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>M1 I1</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Quilted cloth — cheap, quiet, and the layer worn *under* heavier armor. Barely there, but better than skin.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-leather"><h3>Leather</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>torso, arms</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>M1 I2</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>60</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Hardened hide. Turns blunt force better than edges; no real penalty to wear all day.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-mail"><h3>Mail</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>torso, arms, legs</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>M3 I1</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>−1 AG</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>11</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>400</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Interlinked rings — excellent against cuts, poor against crushing impact (that's what the padding under it is for).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-plate"><h3>Plate</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>full body</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>M4 I3</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>−1 AG, −1 PC</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>1500</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Articulated full plate — the best pre-gunpowder protection. Heavy, dulls perception in the helm, and every joint is an adjective.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-shield"><h3>Shield</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>as positioned</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>+1 Parry</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>one hand</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>40</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Not worn but wielded — a Parry PM and cover you can point at the threat. Costs you a hand; see Melee Combat.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-ballistic-vest"><h3>Ballistic Vest</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>torso</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>B3 M2</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>500</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Concealable soft armor — stops handgun rounds and fragments, does little against a rifle. Absorbs (A); doesn't stop penetrators (P).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-tactical-armor"><h3>Tactical Armor</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>torso, groin, neck</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>B4 M3</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>−1 AG</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>9</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>1200</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Soft armor plus rifle-rated hard plates. Bulky, hot, and the difference between a wound level and a funeral.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-riot-gear"><h3>Riot Gear</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>full body</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>I4 M2</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>−1 AG, −1 PC</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>800</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Built for impact — batons, thrown objects, crowds. Great against blunt force, indifferent to bullets and blades.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-combat-armor"><h3>Combat Armor</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>full body, sealed</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>B5 M4 I4</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>−1 PC</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>10</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>7</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>5k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Composite hard-shell suit with its own air — the SF soldier's plate. Light for what it stops; the helm still costs you some perception.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="armor-powered-armor"><h3>Powered Armor</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>full body, sealed</dd><dt>Protection</dt><dd>B6 M6 I6</dd><dt>Absorb</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Penalty</dt><dd>+AG, +ST</dd><dt>Weight</dt><dd>60</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>40k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Motorized exoskeleton — the servos carry the weight *and* add strength, so the penalty inverts. Uses Damage Scale; a walking vehicle you wear.</p></section></div></div></foresight-table>
