# Vehicles
<!--{ "parent": "world", "order": 5 }-->

*A vehicle is an [object](/equipment/) you travel in. Ground, water, and air share one stat block; **spacecraft are vehicles too**, split onto their [own page](/spacecraft/) because their drives define whole settings.*

**Cruise** is the comfortable all-day speed; **Max** is the redline. **Terrain** says where those speeds hold — a road car divides its speed on rough ground, an off-roader barely notices. **Passengers** and **Cargo** are capacity. As with every object, the interesting variety is adjectives: *sporty*, *luxury*, *police*, *cheap/rusty* — see the Vehicle Modification set on the [Equipment](/equipment/) page. Travel time, pursuit, and crashes run off these numbers rather than a separate subsystem.

