center">90 km/h</td><td align="center">130 km/h</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">5</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vehicle-speedboat">Speedboat</a></td><td>water</td><td align="center">40 km/h</td><td align="center">90 km/h</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">5</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vehicle-sailing-ship">Sailing Ship</a></td><td>water</td><td align="center">15 km/h</td><td align="center">25 km/h</td><td align="center">40</td><td align="center">2</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vehicle-helicopter">Helicopter</a></td><td>air</td><td align="center">220 km/h</td><td align="center">300 km/h</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">5</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vehicle-light-aircraft">Light Aircraft</a></td><td>air</td><td align="center">250 km/h</td><td align="center">350 km/h</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">5</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vehicle-airliner">Airliner</a></td><td>air</td><td align="center">900 km/h</td><td align="center">950 km/h</td><td align="center">200</td><td align="center">6</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vehicle-aircar">Aircar</a></td><td>air</td><td align="center">200 km/h</td><td align="center">400 km/h</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">7</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="ev-cards"><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-riding-horse"><h3>Riding Horse</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>ground</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>10 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>50 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>off-road</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>40 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>300</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The original vehicle — self-fuelling, cross-country, and a character in its own right. A *warhorse* (destrier) is one adjective on this noun.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-cart-wagon"><h3>Cart / Wagon</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>ground</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>6 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>15 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>road</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>500 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>150</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Animal-drawn hauler. Slow, roads-only when loaded, but it moves the cargo a party can't carry.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-motorcycle"><h3>Motorcycle</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>ground</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>90 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>180 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>road</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>20 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>8k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Fast, nimble, exposed. Best Maneuver rating on the road and no protection at all when it goes wrong.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-sedan"><h3>Sedan</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>ground</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>100 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>180 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>road</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>80 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>25k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The default car. *Sporty*, *luxury*, *police*, and *cheap/rusty* are all adjectives — see the Vehicle Modification table.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-off-road-4-4"><h3>Off-Road (4×4)</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>ground</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>80 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>150 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>all-terrain</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>300 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>35k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Trades top speed for a terrain value that laughs at mud and rock. The expedition workhorse.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-truck"><h3>Truck</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>ground</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>90 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>130 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>road</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>10 t</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>60k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Heavy road hauler. Slow to accelerate, ponderous to turn, and it carries what nothing else here can.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-speedboat"><h3>Speedboat</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>water</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>40 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>90 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>water</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>200 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>40k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>standard, modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Planing hull — fast on flat water, brutal in chop. The chase vehicle for anywhere with a coastline.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-sailing-ship"><h3>Sailing Ship</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>water</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>15 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>25 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>open water</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>40</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>100 t</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>50k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>ancient, fantasy</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Wind-powered blue-water vessel — crew-hungry, weather-dependent, and the reason the map has other continents on it.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-helicopter"><h3>Helicopter</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>air</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>220 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>300 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>air / VTOL</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>500 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>500k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Vertical take-off, hover, and land where there's no runway. Skilled to fly, thirsty, and loud enough to end any surprise.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-light-aircraft"><h3>Light Aircraft</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>air</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>250 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>350 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>air</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>100 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>200k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Small fixed-wing plane — needs a strip to land, uses terrain value only against where it puts down.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-airliner"><h3>Airliner</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>air</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>900 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>950 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>air</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>200</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>20 t</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>modern</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Long-haul passenger jet. Not a PC's to drive, but it's how everyone gets to the adventure.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="vehicle-aircar"><h3>Aircar</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Domain</dt><dd>air</dd><dt>Cruise</dt><dd>200 km/h</dd><dt>Max</dt><dd>400 km/h</dd><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>air / hover</dd><dt>Passengers</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Cargo</dt><dd>100 kg</dd><dt>TL</dt><dd>7</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd>80k</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Grav or ducted-fan personal flyer — the SF sedan. Point-to-point, no roads, a licence and an autopilot away from trivial.</p></section></div></div></foresight-table>
