<foresight-table src="spacecraft.json" columns="[{&quot;prop&quot;:&quot;name&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Craft&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:180},{&quot;prop&quot;:&quot;setting&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Setting&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:130},{&quot;prop&quot;:&quot;class&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Class&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:120},{&quot;prop&quot;:&quot;drive&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Drive&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:150},{&quot;prop&quot;:&quot;crew&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Crew&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:72,&quot;align&quot;:&quot;center&quot;}]"><div class="ev-static"><table class="ev-table"><thead><tr><th>Craft</th><th>Setting</th><th>Class</th><th>Drive</th><th align="center">Crew</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="#craft-system-fighter">System Fighter</a></td><td>Space Opera</td><td>starfighter</td><td>Ion + hyperdrive</td><td align="center">1</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-light-freighter">Light Freighter</a></td><td>Space Opera</td><td>freighter</td><td>Ion + hyperdrive</td><td align="center">2</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-capital-dreadnought">Capital Dreadnought</a></td><td>Space Opera</td><td>capital</td><td>Ion + hyperdrive</td><td align="center">8000</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-exploration-cruiser">Exploration Cruiser</a></td><td>Warp</td><td>capital</td><td>Warp field</td><td align="center">400</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-shuttle-runabout">Shuttle / Runabout</a></td><td>Warp</td><td>shuttle</td><td>Warp field (short-legged)</td><td align="center">2</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-gate-portal">Gate Portal</a></td><td>Warp</td><td>installation</td><td>Fixed wormhole gate</td><td align="center">—</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-torch-freighter">Torch Freighter</a></td><td>Newtonian</td><td>freighter</td><td>Fusion torch</td><td align="center">6</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-corvette-torch">Corvette (Torch)</a></td><td>Newtonian</td><td>warship</td><td>Fusion torch</td><td align="center">20</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-mass-shunt-tug">Mass-Shunt Tug</a></td><td>Newtonian</td><td>utility</td><td>Fusion torch + mass-shunt</td><td align="center">4</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-general-systems-vehicle">General Systems Vehicle</a></td><td>Culture</td><td>world-ship</td><td>Hyperspace field drive</td><td align="center">millions</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-fast-picket">Fast Picket</a></td><td>Culture</td><td>warship</td><td>Hyperspace field drive</td><td align="center">1 Mind + avatars</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#craft-effector-drone">Effector Drone</a></td><td>Culture</td><td>drone</td><td>Antigrav / field</td><td align="center">1 (itself)</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="ev-cards"><section class="ev-card" id="craft-system-fighter"><h3>System Fighter</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Space Opera</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>starfighter</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Ion + hyperdrive</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>very high thrust, flies in atmosphere</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>instant jump</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Single-seat dogfighter. Space is an ocean and this is a Spitfire — banks, stalls, and turns like an aeroplane because the setting wants it to. Hyperdrive for the jump between scenes.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-light-freighter"><h3>Light Freighter</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Space Opera</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>freighter</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Ion + hyperdrive</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>moderate thrust, atmospheric</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>instant jump</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The scoundrel's ship — small hold, oversized engines, a gun turret, and a hyperdrive that's always one bad roll from failing. The party's home.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-capital-dreadnought"><h3>Capital Dreadnought</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Space Opera</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>capital</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Ion + hyperdrive</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>ponderous</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>instant jump</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>8000</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Kilometre-scale wedge bristling with batteries and fighter bays. Uses Damage Scale wholesale — a setpiece, not a stat line you dogfight.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-exploration-cruiser"><h3>Exploration Cruiser</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Warp</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>capital</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Warp field</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>impulse (fractional-c)</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>warp cruise (superluminal)</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>400</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">A flying town: labs, families, a captain who talks first. FTL is a *cruise speed*, not a jump, so travel time is a plot dial the GM turns.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-shuttle-runabout"><h3>Shuttle / Runabout</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Warp</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>shuttle</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Warp field (short-legged)</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>impulse</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>low warp</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The away-team car — atmosphere-capable, modest warp, the vehicle that actually gets characters to the surface.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-gate-portal"><h3>Gate Portal</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Warp</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>installation</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Fixed wormhole gate</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>instant, gate-to-gate only</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>—</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Not a ship — a doorway. You can only go where a gate already stands, which makes the *map of gates* the campaign map. Stargate-style FTL.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-torch-freighter"><h3>Torch Freighter</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Newtonian</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>freighter</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Fusion torch</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>constant ~⅓ g burn, flip-and-decelerate</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>none</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>6</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Hard-SF hauler à la ForeSight's own physics (and The Expanse): you burn toward your target, flip at the midpoint, and burn to stop. No FTL — the solar system *is* the setting.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-corvette-torch"><h3>Corvette (Torch)</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Newtonian</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>warship</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Fusion torch</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>high-g burn, railguns + torpedoes</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>none</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Newtonian warship: no shields, no banking — just delta-v, point-defence, and the tyranny of the rocket equation. Combat is about vectors and reaction mass.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-mass-shunt-tug"><h3>Mass-Shunt Tug</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Newtonian</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>utility</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Fusion torch + mass-shunt</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>torch</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>shunt between fixed jump points</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">ForeSight's original FTL: the *mass shunt* throws a ship between fixed points (a magic gate serves the same role in a fantasy-SF setting). Torch drive does everything in-system; the shunt links the stars.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-general-systems-vehicle"><h3>General Systems Vehicle</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Culture</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>world-ship</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Hyperspace field drive</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>near-c trivially</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>near-instant, engine-grid powered</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>millions</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">A sentient Mind wearing a ship the size of a country, home to millions and able to build more of itself. Post-scarcity: 'stats' are whatever the Mind decides. The setting where the ship is the most powerful *character*.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-fast-picket"><h3>Fast Picket</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Culture</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>warship</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Hyperspace field drive</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>absurd</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>near-instant</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>1 Mind + avatars</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">A small, appallingly fast, appallingly armed Mind. Diplomacy-by-presence; when one arrives, the scene is already over. Effectors and gridfire sit far off any mundane Damage Scale.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="craft-effector-drone"><h3>Effector Drone</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Setting</dt><dd>Culture</dd><dt>Class</dt><dd>drone</dd><dt>Drive</dt><dd>Antigrav / field</dd><dt>Sublight</dt><dd>flight</dd><dt>FTL</dt><dd>carried</dd><dt>Crew</dt><dd>1 (itself)</dd><dt>Tags</dt><dd>sf</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">A sentient, fist-to-suitcase-sized machine — companion, bodyguard, and party member. The Culture's answer to 'what does a PC-scale piece of tech look like when it's also a person?'</p></section></div></div></foresight-table>
</div>
