description, so long as it is in the same plane as the invoker, a desire to travel as quickly as it is safely able to the point the invoker occupied at the time of invocation (<strong>fixed</strong>).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-animate-dead"><h3>Animate Dead</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§20A4</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>summon</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Animate the corpse or skeleton of a DT1 or weaker creature (by summoning a trivial demon for the purpose) as a zombie or skeleton respectively (see the creature descriptions). Note: the figures given (under Creatures) for zombies/skeletons assume that (near-)human skeletons/corpses are being animated. If the original creature had DT d, then the skeleton/zombie will have DT d-3 / d+1, and DC d+1 / d+2. The GM may wish to make special allowance for non-humanoid skeletons/zombies. Also note that skeletons and zombies are intrinsically hostile to any living creature (including their summoner). Corpses/skeletons without intact heads/skulls cannot be animated.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-named-summons"><h3>Named Summons</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§20A4</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>summon</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Give a specifically designated creature (one whose personal name and appearance can be uniquely specified), wherever it is on whatever plane, a desire to travel as quickly as it is safely able to the point the invoker occupied at the time of invocation (<strong>fixed</strong>).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-dismissal"><h3>Dismissal</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§20A5</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>summon</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Dismiss a creature which fails an EF 7-2B WP roll (use magic resistance lacking a WP value) of DT ≤ ⌊A/2⌋, giving it an overpowering urge to return to its &quot;home&quot; (plane, lair, or whatever). If it has no means to do 